// The global `Map` in packages/engine/src (ADR 0020, plan §I.1). It is a plugin of its own, not
// a noRestrictedGlobals entry, so that one file can be excepted without repeating the engine's
// list of denied globals: an override replaces a rule's options instead of merging them, while
// Biome adds up the plugins of every override that matches a file and cannot take one away.
// biome.json registers it for src except canonical/value.ts, which looks up the objects a walk
// entered, and step/context.ts, which looks up the draw sequences of a tick; neither iterates a
// Map.
// It reports every reference to the name outside a type (member access, calls, `new`, aliasing,
// arguments, shorthand properties, and `typeof`), even where a local declaration shadows the
// global. Property names, keys, and type positions are not references to the global, and
// noGlobalAssign rejects assignments to it everywhere. tests/repo/engine-lint.test.ts proves both
// sides and the exact extent of the exception.
// It is also registered for packages/agents/src, with no exception (ADR 0023).
language js

JsReferenceIdentifier() as $reference where {
  $reference <: r"^Map$",
  not $reference <: within or {
    TsReferenceType(),
    TsTypeofType()
  },
  register_diagnostic(span=$reference, message="The global `Map` is denied outside canonical/value.ts and step/context.ts: a Map iterates in insertion order, which a resumed world may not share; iterate records in canonical order (plan §I.1).")
}
